><h1>Photovoltaics in DIY retail: Solar power for BAUHAUS in Stuttgart-Unte=
rt=C3=BCrkheim</h1><div class=3D"div spacer-medium"></div><p class=3D"text-=
size-medium">How can the high energy requirements in the DIY sector be met =
sustainably? At its Stuttgart-Untert=C3=BCrkheim location, BAUHAUS, togethe=
r with Nanz Handelsimmobilien and GIGA.GREEN, is demonstrating how large ro=
of areas can be turned into efficient energy sources. With over 1,300 solar=
 modules and an output of around 590 kWp, the store produces a large part o=
f its own electricity =E2=80=94 and reduces its CO=E2=82=82 emissions by mo=
re than 5,600 tons in the long term.</p></div></div><div style=3D"backgroun=
d-image:url(&quot;https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/66506dbcb087075928b5a2=
c8/68f5a4024beb03e20f0cde1f_DJI_0914.jpg&quot;)" class=3D"blog-post1-header=
