ss=3D"blog-post1-content_content"><div class=3D"text-rich-text text-color-g=
reen text-size-medium w-richtext"><h2><strong>Energy for large areas</stron=
g></h2><p>DIY retailers and home improvement stores are among the commercia=
l properties with particularly high electricity consumption. Lighting, vent=
ilation, heating, and large sales areas continuously drive up energy requir=
ements. At the same time, operators and tenants are under pressure to reduc=
e emissions and ensure predictable energy costs in the long term. At its St=
uttgart-Untert=C3=BCrkheim location, BAUHAUS, together with Nanz Handelsimm=
obilien and GIGA.GREEN, is demonstrating how photovoltaics can help meet th=
ese challenges.</p><h2><strong>Starting point: Sustainability as a location=
 factor</strong></h2><p>The owner, Nanz Handelsimmobilien, has been relying=
 on solar energy for years to future-proof its properties. With BAUHAUS in =
Stuttgart-Untert=C3=BCrkheim, another large DIY retailer has now been solar=
ized=E2=80=94as part of a clear strategy to transform roof space into valua=
ble energy sources and increase attractiveness for tenants.</p><h2><strong>=
Solution: Photovoltaics on the roof of the BAUHAUS site</strong></h2><p>A h=
igh-performance photovoltaic system was installed on the roof of the BAUHAU=
S site in Untert=C3=BCrkheim. It produces renewable energy directly on site=
 and delivers tangible benefits for both owners and tenants. Key data for t=
he project:</p><ul role=3D"list"><li><strong>589.05 kWp installed PV capaci=
ty</strong></li><li><strong>1,386 solar modules installed</strong></li><li>=
<strong>5,654 tons of CO=E2=82=82 reduction in total</strong></li></ul><p>=
=E2=80=8D</p><figure style=3D"padding-bottom:56.206088992974244%" class=3D"=
w-richtext-align-fullwidth w-richtext-figure-type-video"><div><iframe src=
=3D"cid:frame-AEE9CD5A21A684C0788FF879BF42D9F9@mhtml.blink" title=3D"GIGA.G=
REEN | BAUHAUS Fachcentrum in Stuttgart-Untert=C3=BCrkheim" scrolling=3D"no=
" frameborder=3D"0" allowfullscreen=3D"true" data-lf-form-tracking-inspecte=
d-laxoeak26p04oygd=3D"true" data-lf-yt-playback-inspected-laxoeak26p04oygd=
=3D"true" data-lf-vimeo-playback-inspected-laxoeak26p04oygd=3D"true"></ifra=
me></div></figure><p>=E2=80=8D</p><h2><strong>Results: Economic efficiency =
and sustainability combined</strong></h2><p>The photovoltaic system allows =
the DIY retailer to plan its electricity costs for the long term using the =
onsite PPA model. At the same time, the project significantly reduces the s=
ite's emissions and increases the property value through a future-proof ene=
rgy supply.</p><h2><strong>Customer feedback</strong></h2><p>=E2=80=9CDIY r=
etailers require large areas of space=E2=80=94and these areas offer ideal c=
onditions for photovoltaics. This allows us to transform roof space into a =
valuable source of energy, reduce operating costs for our tenants, and incr=
ease the value of our properties at the same time. =E2=80=9D</p><p><strong>=
Florian Nanz, Nanz Retail Properties GmbH</strong><br><br>=E2=80=9CThe phot=
ovoltaic system enables us to secure stable electricity prices in the long =
term, reduce emissions at our Stuttgart-Untert=C3=BCrkheim site, and at the=
 same time strengthen our customers' confidence in our commitment to sustai=
nability. =E2=80=9D</p><p><strong>Giancarlo Posella, BAUHAUS Technical Cent=
er Stuttgart-Untert=C3=BCrkheim</strong></p><h2><strong>Conclusion: Photovo=
ltaics as a model for retail</strong></h2><p>The example in Stuttgart-Unter=
t=C3=BCrkheim shows how photovoltaics can turn retail properties into susta=
inable and economically stable locations. While owners future-proof their p=
ortfolios, tenants benefit directly from predictable energy costs and a bet=
ter carbon footprint. Photovoltaics is therefore key to strengthening the c=
ompetitiveness of retail properties.</p><figure class=3D"w-richtext-align-c=
enter w-richtext-figure-type-image"><div><img loading=3D"lazy" alt=3D"" src=
=3D"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/66506dbcb087075928b5a2c8/68f5a4024be=
